From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: size coherent mailboxes for WLAN statistics

The Connac2 GET 2 receive-statistics command exchanges 0x1250 bytes,
including the eight-byte WLAN header. The 256-byte coherent mailbox
rejects this request before publishing it to the NPU.

Reserve SZ_8K per core at probe, the next power of two covering the
4688-byte command. Keep the existing bounded sender, per-core lock and
coherent buffer lifetime; the atomic submission path still reuses its
buffer. Eight cores reserve 64 KiB total. The 8192-byte limit fits the
firmware's 16-bit mailbox length and the existing 32-bit coherent DMA
mask continues to constrain the entire allocation.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/of_platform.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
+#include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 
 #include "airoha_eth.h"
@@ -28,11 +29,10 @@
 #define NPU_EN7581_FIRMWARE_DATA_MAX_SIZE	0x10000
 #define NPU_DUMP_SIZE				512
 /*
- * Mailbox DMA payload size. Covers sizeof(struct ppe_mbox_data) (28) and
- * WLAN TLV messages (header + payload); largest in-tree WLAN payload today
- * is 16 bytes (INODE_TXRX_REG_ADDR). Keep headroom for future commands.
+ * Connac2 WLAN GET 2 statistics uses 0x1250 bytes including its header.
+ * Reserve one coherent buffer per core at probe; submission can be atomic.
  */
-#define AIROHA_NPU_MBOX_SIZE			256
+#define AIROHA_NPU_MBOX_SIZE			SZ_8K
 #define AIROHA_NPU_MBOX_TIMEOUT_US		(100 * USEC_PER_MSEC)
 
 #define REG_NPU_LOCAL_SRAM		0x0
